-- akn:art_4__para_4-2 Attaches annexes A, B and C; the circular as the corpus holds it does not print them (tables of those letters and dates are in the corpus's tables collection, not vendored here), so the table in force is named above and its figures are an input.
-- akn:art_4__para_4-4 Attaches annex D; the circular as the corpus holds it does not print it (a table of that letter and date is in the corpus's tables collection, not vendored here), so the table in force is named above and its figures are an input.
-- akn:art_11__para_11-7 The union's statement that the section admits no error in any salary; no rule.

-- The Ministry's note: how many of the new roles a principal may choose,
-- in addition to the upper division's existing roles.
@ref akn:art_14__para_14-2__hc_1 akn:art_14__para_14-2__hc_1__subpara_14-2-1 akn:art_14__para_14-2__hc_1__subpara_14-2-2 akn:art_14__para_14-2__hc_1__subpara_14-2-3
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `new roles a principal may choose` `the day` IS
    IF `the day` AT LEAST Date 1 9 2021
    THEN 3
    ELSE IF `the day` AT LEAST Date 1 9 2020
         THEN 2
         ELSE IF `the day` AT LEAST Date 1 9 2019
              THEN 1
              ELSE 0

-- The Women's Work Law (through the agreement of 14.3.2018): §17(ה) and
-- (ז) count a month of the birth and parenthood period as work for the
-- grant, as unpaid leave after it is not, and §17(ו) takes the position on
-- its eve. The period harms no right that turns on seniority (§6(ט)). The
-- floor is met.
`§17 of תשע"ח/3 counts the birth and parenthood period, as the Women's Work Law keeps it` MEANS
    `§17 of 14.3.2018 counts the birth and parenthood period, as the Women's Work Law keeps it`
#ASSERT `§17 of תשע"ח/3 counts the birth and parenthood period, as the Women's Work Law keeps it`


-- Against the Minimum Wage Law's floor (MMS-601): §6 (the merger agreement's new 5א(ה))
-- leaves the merger supplement out, and 17(ט) the one-time grant;
-- leaving them out of the pay that counts toward the top-up makes the
-- top-up the law's or more (its §11). Checked on a month's figures as if
-- §3 counted each (a fixed supplement for the work), the strictest case.
#ASSERT NOT `counting a component as the instrument does falls below the Minimum Wage Law` 5300 4800 (`component paid in the month under the Minimum Wage Law` `a fixed supplement paid for the work, under section 3(ב)(3)` 300) (`the merger supplement counts for` `topping up to the minimum wage`)
#ASSERT NOT `counting a component as the instrument does falls below the Minimum Wage Law` 5300 4800 (`component paid in the month under the Minimum Wage Law` `a fixed supplement paid for the work, under section 3(ב)(3)` 300) (`the grant counts for` `topping up to the minimum wage`)

§§ `18 שכר המנהלים`

-- §18a: the parties go on negotiating how to allocate the budget agreed for
-- principals' pay. §18b: failing an agreement by 1.4.2018, the "87
-- transition" supplement rises by 460 from 1.9.2018 (to 548.52) and by
-- another 460 from 1.9.2019 (to 1,008.52).
@ref akn:art_18__para_a
`the parties go on negotiating the allocation of the budget for principals' pay` MEANS TRUE

-- §18b is the agreement's §18(ב), word for word: its rule, imported.
@ref akn:art_18__para_b akn:art_18__para_b__subpara_1 akn:art_18__para_b__subpara_2
GIVEN `an allocation agreement signed by 1.4.2018` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the 87 transition supplement under section 18b` `an allocation agreement signed by 1.4.2018` `the day` IS
    `the 87 transition supplement under §18(ב)` `an allocation agreement signed by 1.4.2018` `the day`

-- §18b's last words: with no agreement by 1.4.2018, no further negotiation
-- on that cost is held.
GIVEN `an allocation agreement signed by 1.4.2018` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `no further negotiation on the cost` `an allocation agreement signed by 1.4.2018` IF
    NOT `an allocation agreement signed by 1.4.2018`

-- akn:art_18__para_c A further circular will be published as needed; no rule.

§§ `19 החזר ימי לימודים בשל שביתה`

DECLARE `make-up day` IS ONE OF
    `the day after Shavuot, 21.5.2018`
    `Lag BaOmer, 3.5.2018`
    `the day after Sukkot, 2.10.2018`

@desc An upper division and one of its teaching employees, as far as the make-up days ask.
DECLARE `struck school and teacher` HAS
    `school struck on a general strike day`  IS A BOOLEAN @desc 12.11.2017 or 21.11.2017
    `local strike days at the school`        IS A NUMBER  @desc full days of strike after the general strike days, in November or December 2017
    `lessons missed on the day chosen for Shavuot` IS A NUMBER @desc on 12.11.2017 or 21.11.2017, as the principal chose, by the general strike
    `lessons missed on general strike days`  IS A NUMBER
    `lessons missed on local strike days`    IS A NUMBER
    `lessons made up after Shavuot`          IS A NUMBER
    `lessons made up on Lag BaOmer`          IS A NUMBER

-- §19.1: by the Director-General's notice of 14.3.2018 the Ministry orders
-- make-up school days in the upper divisions that struck.
@ref akn:art_19__para_19-1 akn:art_19__para_19-1__subpara_a akn:art_19__para_19-1__subpara_a__cls_1 akn:art_19__para_19-1__subpara_b akn:art_19__para_19-1__subpara_b__cls_1 akn:art_19__para_19-1__subpara_c akn:art_19__para_19-1__subpara_c__cls_1
GIVEN d IS A `make-up day`
      s IS A `struck school and teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the school holds` d s IF
    CONSIDER d
    WHEN `the day after Shavuot, 21.5.2018` THEN s's `school struck on a general strike day`
    WHEN `Lag BaOmer, 3.5.2018` THEN s's `school struck on a general strike day` AND s's `local strike days at the school` AT LEAST 1
    WHEN `the day after Sukkot, 2.10.2018` THEN s's `school struck on a general strike day` OR s's `local strike days at the school` AT LEAST 1

-- §19.1(a)(2): the Shavuot timetable is that of 12.11.2017 or 21.11.2017,
-- as the principal decides — an input (`lessons missed on the day chosen
-- for Shavuot`). §19.1(a)(3): only those absent that day by the general
-- strike, for as many lessons as they missed, and no more.
@ref akn:art_19__para_19-1__subpara_a__cls_2 akn:art_19__para_19-1__subpara_a__cls_3
GIVEN s IS A `struck school and teacher`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `lessons owed after Shavuot` s IS
    s's `lessons missed on the day chosen for Shavuot`

-- §19.1(b)(2)-(4): up to 8 frontal lessons on Lag BaOmer, only for those
-- absent on local strike days, no more than they missed there.
@ref akn:art_19__para_19-1__subpara_b__cls_2 akn:art_19__para_19-1__subpara_b__cls_3 akn:art_19__para_19-1__subpara_b__cls_4
GIVEN s IS A `struck school and teacher`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `lessons owed on Lag BaOmer` s IS
    min (s's `lessons missed on local strike days`) 8

-- §19.1(c)(2)-(4): after Sukkot, up to 8 frontal lessons, for those whose
-- missed lessons exceed those made up, and no more than the difference.
@ref akn:art_19__para_19-1__subpara_c__cls_2 akn:art_19__para_19-1__subpara_c__cls_3 akn:art_19__para_19-1__subpara_c__cls_4
GIVEN s IS A `struck school and teacher`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `lessons owed after Sukkot` s IS
    min (max 0 (s's `lessons missed on general strike days`
                PLUS s's `lessons missed on local strike days`
                MINUS s's `lessons made up after Shavuot`
                MINUS s's `lessons made up on Lag BaOmer`)) 8

-- §19.1(a)(4), (b)(5), (c)(5), (d)(2): each make-up lesson earns the pay
-- withheld for one strike hour; paid with the May 2018 salary (9) for
-- Shavuot and Lag BaOmer, with October 2018's (14) for Sukkot.
@ref akn:art_19__para_19-1__subpara_a__cls_4 akn:art_19__para_19-1__subpara_b__cls_5 akn:art_19__para_19-1__subpara_c__cls_5 akn:art_19__para_19-1__subpara_c__cls_5/p2 akn:art_19__para_19-1__subpara_d__cls_2
GIVEN `lessons made up` IS A NUMBER, `pay withheld for one strike hour` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `make-up pay` `lessons made up` `pay withheld for one strike hour` IS
    `lessons made up` TIMES `pay withheld for one strike hour`

@ref akn:art_19__para_19-1__subpara_a__cls_4 akn:art_19__para_19-1__subpara_b__cls_5
GIVEN `pay due` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `wage action`
DECIDE `paying for the spring make-up days` `pay due` IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `pay for make-up lessons` `amount`
          PROVIDED `amount` AT LEAST `pay due`
    WITHIN 9
    LEST BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "section 19.1: make-up pay for Shavuot and Lag BaOmer with the salary for May 2018"

@ref akn:art_19__para_19-1__subpara_c__cls_5/p2
GIVEN `pay due` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `wage action`
DECIDE `paying for the Sukkot make-up day` `pay due` IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `pay for make-up lessons` `amount`
          PROVIDED `amount` AT LEAST `pay due`
    WITHIN 14
    LEST BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "section 19.1(c)(5): make-up pay for the day after Sukkot with the salary for October 2018"

-- §19.1(d): teachers in a school with more than one local strike day, who
-- made up lessons on Lag BaOmer and still missed more than they made up,
-- may make up frontal and individual hours during תשע"ח as the principal
-- decides.
@ref akn:art_19__para_19-1__subpara_d akn:art_19__para_19-1__subpara_d__cls_1 akn:art_19__para_19-1__subpara_d__cls_2/p2 akn:art_19__para_19-1__subpara_d__cls_2__pnt_a akn:art_19__para_19-1__subpara_d__cls_2__pnt_b akn:art_19__para_19-1__subpara_d__cls_2__pnt_c
GIVEN s IS A `struck school and teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may make up further hours in תשע"ח` s IF
        s's `local strike days at the school` GREATER THAN 1
    AND s's `school struck on a general strike day`
    AND s's `lessons made up on Lag BaOmer` GREATER THAN 0
    AND s's `lessons missed on local strike days` GREATER THAN s's `lessons made up on Lag BaOmer`

-- §19.2: an advance with the April 2018 salary (8): the general-strike
-- deduction, plus the deduction for the first local strike day.
@ref akn:art_19__para_19-2 akn:art_19__para_19-2/p1 akn:art_19__para_19-2__subpara_a akn:art_19__para_19-2__subpara_b
GIVEN `struck on a general strike day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `general strike deduction` IS A NUMBER
      `struck on a local strike day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `first local strike day deduction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the strike advance` `struck on a general strike day` `general strike deduction` `struck on a local strike day` `first local strike day deduction` IS
    (IF `struck on a general strike day` THEN `general strike deduction` ELSE 0)
    PLUS (IF `struck on a local strike day` THEN `first local strike day deduction` ELSE 0)

@ref akn:art_19__para_19-2/p1
GIVEN `advance due` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `wage action`
DECIDE `paying the strike advance` `advance due` IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `pay the advance` `amount`
          PROVIDED `amount` AT LEAST `advance due`
    WITHIN 8
    LEST BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "section 19.2: the advance is paid with the salary for April 2018"

-- §19.2(c): the advance is recovered with the May 2018 salary (9) up to the
-- spring make-up pay, the rest with October 2018's (14); for one on unpaid
-- leave or sabbatical in תשע"ט, with May and August 2018 (12); on leaving,
-- from the last salary and any payment due.
-- not weighed against `the Advance Notice Law`: 19.2(ג) names the end of the relation
-- only as when the advance not yet deducted is deducted, from the last
-- salary and any payment owed; it gives or asks no notice, so it rules
-- nothing the law puts a floor under.
@ref akn:art_19__para_19-2__subpara_c akn:art_19__para_19-2__subpara_c/p2
GIVEN `advance` IS A NUMBER, `spring make-up pay` IS A NUMBER, `on leave or sabbatical in תשע"ט` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `advance recovery`
DECIDE `recovering the strike advance` `advance` `spring make-up pay` `on leave or sabbatical in תשע"ט` IS
    LIST `advance recovery` 9 (min `advance` `spring make-up pay`),
         `advance recovery` (IF `on leave or sabbatical in תשע"ט` THEN 12 ELSE 14) (max 0 (`advance` MINUS `spring make-up pay`))

DECLARE `advance recovery` HAS
    `salary month of recovery` IS A NUMBER
    `amount recovered` IS A NUMBER

-- §19.2(c), last sentence: if the employment ends before the advance is
-- wholly recovered, the rest is deducted from the last month's salary
-- before it ends, and against any payment the employer owes the employee.
GIVEN `the rest of the advance` IS A NUMBER, `the last salary month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `advance recovery`
DECIDE `recovering the rest on leaving` `the rest of the advance` `the last salary month` IS
    `advance recovery` `the last salary month` `the rest of the advance`

-- §19.3: the Ministry issues guidelines to principals (no date given).
@ref akn:art_19__para_19-3
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `wage action`
DECIDE `the Ministry's guidelines` IS
    PARTY `the Ministry of Education`
    MUST  `issue implementation guidelines to principals`


-- akn:conclusions The contact line for questions, the list of enclosures (annexes A to E and the agreement, none printed in the circular; the corpus holds an agreement of 14.3.2018 between the local authorities and ארגון המורים, agreements/oz-latmura/2018-03-14_oz-latmura_wage-agreement-2017-2022.xml, not yet encoded), the sign-off and the copies list; no rule.

-- Against the Wage Protection Law (MMS-601): §11.5 deems an overpayment an
-- advance on wages for §25(א)(7), and §11.6 deducts it in twelve equal
-- parts — within §25 for any overpayment up to three months' wages, and
-- above that §11.5's own words, "for §25(א)(7)", carry the cap on the
-- rest, as with §93 of the completion agreement of 29.2.2012. §19.2(ג)
-- recovers the strike advance "בהתאם לחוק הגנת השכר": an advance on
-- wages, of a few days' pay, which §25(א)(7) lets be deducted whole in
-- each of its two months; and on leaving, §25(ב) lets the rest be
-- deducted from the last wage.
#ASSERT `the overpayment counts as an advance on wages` 12 TRUE
#ASSERT `section 25 of the Wage Protection Law permits the deduction` `an advance on account of wages`
#ASSERT `equal monthly parts of the advance stay within section 25` 30000 10000 12
#ASSERT `the most section 25 lets be deducted of advances this month` 1500 10000 0 EQUALS 1500
#ASSERT `what section 25(ב) lets be deducted from the last wage` TRUE 700 8000 EQUALS 700

§§ `Findings`

-- F-2017-18_tashach_03-a: §18b allocates "the cost under subsections
-- (a)(1) and (a)(2) above"; §18a has no (1) or (2).
`the subparagraphs §18a has` MEANS 0
`the subparagraphs §18b cites in §18a` MEANS 2
`section 18b cites subparagraphs section 18a does not have` MEANS
    `the subparagraphs §18b cites in §18a` GREATER THAN `the subparagraphs §18a has`
#ASSERT `section 18b cites subparagraphs section 18a does not have`

-- F-2017-18_tashach_03-b: §11.1-§11.2 bind "sections 5.2 and 5.3"
-- together with the rest; section 5 is lettered (a)-(c) and has no 5.2 or 5.3.
`the provisions of section 5` MEANS LIST "5(a)", "5(b)", "5(c)"
`section 11 names provisions section 5 does not have` MEANS
    (NOT elem "5.2" `the provisions of section 5`) AND NOT elem "5.3" `the provisions of section 5`
#ASSERT `section 11 names provisions section 5 does not have`

-- F-2017-18_tashach_03-c: §8.1 computes on "the combined salary (under
-- section 3 above)"; section 3 is the definitions, the tables are section 4.
DECLARE `section of this circular` IS ONE OF
    `section 3 definitions`, `section 4 combined-salary tables`, `section 6 merger supplement`
`what section 8.1 cites for the combined salary` MEANS `section 3 definitions`
`section 8.1 cites the definitions for the combined salary` MEANS
    NOT (`what section 8.1 cites for the combined salary` EQUALS `section 4 combined-salary tables`)
#ASSERT `section 8.1 cites the definitions for the combined salary`

-- F-2017-18_tashach_03-d: the mentor stipend has no base for a principal.
`a principal mentor has no stipend base` MEANS
        isNothing (`the mentor stipend base` `a principal not in the reform` 10000 0 160 1900)
    AND isNothing (`the mentor stipend base` `a principal in the reform` 10000 2000 0 0)
#ASSERT `a principal mentor has no stipend base`

§§ `Worked examples`

#ASSERT `new roles a principal may choose` (Date 1 10 2020) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the 87 transition supplement under section 18b` FALSE (Date 1 10 2019) EQUALS JUST 1008.52

`a teacher in a school that struck twice locally` MEANS `struck school and teacher` WITH
    `school struck on a general strike day` IS TRUE
    `local strike days at the school`       IS 2
    `lessons missed on the day chosen for Shavuot` IS 5
    `lessons missed on general strike days` IS 10
    `lessons missed on local strike days`   IS 12
    `lessons made up after Shavuot`         IS 5
    `lessons made up on Lag BaOmer`         IS 8

#ASSERT `lessons owed after Sukkot` `a teacher in a school that struck twice locally` EQUALS 8
#ASSERT `the school holds` `Lag BaOmer, 3.5.2018` `a teacher in a school that struck twice locally`
#ASSERT `may make up further hours in תשע"ח` `a teacher in a school that struck twice locally`

§§ `Property checks`

-- §14's note: the principal's choice of roles never falls with time and
-- reaches three.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN d YIELD `new roles a principal may choose` d AT MOST `new roles a principal may choose` (Date 1 1 2022)) `the days checked`
#ASSERT `new roles a principal may choose` (Date 1 1 2022) EQUALS 3

-- §18b over the days: no amount with an agreement; without one, 548.52
-- from 1.9.2018 and 1,008.52 from 1.9.2019, each 460 above the last.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN d YIELD `the 87 transition supplement under section 18b` TRUE d EQUALS NOTHING) `the days checked`
#ASSERT `the 87 transition supplement under section 18b` FALSE (Date 1 9 2018) EQUALS JUST (88.52 PLUS 460)
#ASSERT `the 87 transition supplement under section 18b` FALSE (Date 1 9 2019) EQUALS JUST (88.52 PLUS 920)

GIVEN g IS A BOOLEAN
      l IS A NUMBER
      x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `struck school and teacher`
DECIDE `a checked school` g l x IS
    `struck school and teacher` WITH
        `school struck on a general strike day` IS g
        `local strike days at the school`       IS l
        `lessons missed on the day chosen for Shavuot` IS x
        `lessons missed on general strike days` IS x
        `lessons missed on local strike days`   IS x
        `lessons made up after Shavuot`         IS min x 4
        `lessons made up on Lag BaOmer`         IS min x 8

-- §19.1 over strikes and lessons: Lag BaOmer only where both kinds of
-- strike were held and Sukkot wherever either was; never more than eight
-- lessons owed on Lag BaOmer or after Sukkot.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN g YIELD
                all (GIVEN l YIELD
                        all (GIVEN x YIELD
                                LET s MEANS `a checked school` g l x
                                IN      ((NOT `the school holds` `Lag BaOmer, 3.5.2018` s) OR `the school holds` `the day after Sukkot, 2.10.2018` s)
                                    AND ((NOT `the school holds` `the day after Shavuot, 21.5.2018` s) OR `the school holds` `the day after Sukkot, 2.10.2018` s)
                                    AND `lessons owed on Lag BaOmer` s AT MOST 8
                                    AND `lessons owed after Sukkot` s AT LEAST 0
                                    AND `lessons owed after Sukkot` s AT MOST 8)
                            (range 0 12))
                    (range 0 3))
            `both booleans`

-- §19.2 over advances and spring pay: the two recoveries add up to the
-- advance, the first never above the spring pay.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN a YIELD
                all (GIVEN p YIELD
                        all (GIVEN o YIELD
                                LET r MEANS `recovering the strike advance` a p o
                                IN      sum (map (GIVEN x YIELD x's `amount recovered`) r) EQUALS a
                                    AND (at r 0)'s `amount recovered` AT MOST p)
                            `both booleans`)
                    (LIST 0, 200, 500))
            (LIST 0, 300, 600)
